<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The window Android paints while the process starts, before Flutter has
    drawn anything. Removed automatically on the first Flutter frame.

    Two layers: the app's own background colour, and the mark centred on it.

    The mark here is the whole mark, at rest. It used to be an empty tray, for
    a Flutter splash screen that drew the identical empty tray and then filed
    the cards into it — a handover that stopped existing when the router
    started deciding the first destination before `runApp`. There is nothing
    between this window and the first real screen now, so there is nothing for
    an incomplete mark to hand over to.

    `splash_logo` is a real raster now (generated per density by
    `tool/generate_brand_assets.dart`), so wrapping it in <bitmap> is both
    legal and the right form — it is what pins the gravity. It used to be a
    vector, and <bitmap> around a vector fails to inflate; because this
    drawable is the activity's starting window, that failure took the whole app
    down before Flutter ever started.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@color/splash_background" />
    <item>
        <bitmap
            android:src="@drawable/splash_logo"
            android:gravity="center" />
    </item>
</layer-list>
